From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/17] Defer replies the caller does not need

Mapped-memory flushes and fence resets are sent without waiting for their
result. Their 4-byte replies stay queued on the stream and are drained in
order before the next reply is read, so a frame pays one round trip instead of
one per call (caboose-bounded-memory/deferred_replies.h). In-flight deferred
bytes stay under the device link's window.
